{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/619380-domain-panem-et-circenses","id":619380,"title":"Domain: Panem et Circenses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-07T14:01:11-07:00","id":619380,"title":"Domain: Panem et Circenses","content":"Designing a domain set in a fictional city to avoid geographical realism. The city itself is still a work in progress, but I wanted to come up with a premise that would make the domain itself interesting but not so far out of the norm that it's intimidating for new players.<br /> <br /> My first point, which is the most critical to the plot, is that this is a domain that only recently was brought back from the brink of chaos. Elder feuds spiraled out of control, people died. The major players met their final death or fled in the last year. But their pawns still hold grudges.<br /> <br /> Point two: the new Prince is a puppet...sort of. Cheshire, as she calls herself, is a Daeva only a few decades into undeath, and was appointed by a circle of Kindred who despise each other. She's not the strongest, smartest, or best connected Kindred in the city. She was the compromise that left everyone unhappy. She knows all this, and doesn't give a rat's ass.<br /> <br /> She's just enjoying the hell out of it. She doesn't care about the feud between her Primogen, but is smart enough to maintain the balance of power between them, since any one of them could probably take her down if they could survive the wrath of the other four.<br /> <br /> Basically I designed her as a bored, uninvolved, hedonistic Prince who is unliving on borrowed time and can be deposed in play.<br /> <br /> Which leads us to point three...and where Panem et Circenses comes in.<br /> <br /> The Prince doesn't want to deal with matters of state that don't interest her. She's bored easily and concerned with the luxury that power affords her, not power itself. So you want her to oversee a matter? Well, make it worth her time.<br /> <br /> Each Covenent, as well as each Primogen, and some independent coteries, have a specific place where they can host Elysium. Any host can call for the Prince to settle a dispute or hear a plea at their Elysium...but you provide entertainment.<br /> <br /> The Sanctified hold their Elysium in a graveyard chapel where they put on Bloody Passion Plays, sufficiently altered to make them palatable for unbelievers. The Mekhet Primogen hosts in the VIP room of the hottest S&amp;M club in the city, where Kine perform live extreme fetish shows. One Coterie of Drakes makes their shared Haven into a museum of the uncanny and abnormal.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter what kind of entertainment...but if your show isn't sufficiently satisfying, good luck getting your matter across. The Prince may even leave before it's over if she's bored. And if she leaves before the entertainment is over, it's her unspoken decree that for the rest of the night, Elysium--and the protections it affords--are nullified.<br /> <br /> Thus, even the most reserved Kindred need to be gracious hosts and entertainers aside for any political leverage. Have fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7033,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","user":"FunSize","date":". 08-07-2015, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T15:26:29-07:00","id":619511,"title":"","content":"Aside it being extremely cliche with the Daeva, I think this idea would work better with a more powerful Prince.<br /> <br /> She's just some decades into unlife and an unliving weak compromise? Being such a douche would be the quickest way to bring her down. She hurts the city's politics behaving like a child, in a moment when the city desperately needs stability. I an hardly think it would work, even if she's just the &quot;decision that makes everyone unhappy&quot;.<br /> <br /> The trope on inverted Panen et Circensis (where is the Prince who's getting &quot;bread and circus&quot;) is a good one, but you need a stable Domain or an insanely strong Prince for that to be credible. Decadence is born from stability and riches, not from mayhem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T13:06:12-07:00","id":620433,"title":"","content":"Okay I get what you mean there. My thought was the -real- powerful Kindred (mostly the Primogen and a few others) basically know that if they make a move against the Prince, the others will come down on them. So for the time being their respective feuds have gone into cold war, with an incompetent Prince that could easily mismanage the current balance of power. Of course the PCs will likely throw a wrench in that balance after a while.<br /> <br /> Her insurance on mixing politics with pleasure is actually a calculated move on her part. By making the power players spend time, resources, and energy on keeping her entertained, they have less time and resources to move against each other--or her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:18:40-07:00","id":620624,"title":"","content":"The problem is, as things are, they won't. She is a bad compromise, because she hurts even the most basic administrative roles. She is going to upset everyone in the city. This is the single surest way to start a war.<br /> <br /> A character with this kind of behavior needs a safe support to do so, a reason to think she is safe from harm, or to just be spoiled. Because not only he power-players of the city will be upset, the other Kindred will, also. They will want her head. The power-players will see the domain itself falling to pieces as people just ignore or resent her.<br /> <br /> Not to say that this is the behavior of someone who can actually enforce something, and you described a Prince who isn't able to enforce nothing. People would be simply ignoring her, until someone is upset enough to kill her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:32:56-07:00","id":620641,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this misses a point, but maybe the stated scenario is what the majority of the domain <i>thinks</i> is true, when in reality the young Daeva has some secret trump card that lets her stay in power while appearing weak? Like some sort of powerful Majesty/Obfuscate Devotion that makes it difficult for people to consider her as worth acting against or harming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T17:27:27-07:00","id":620746,"title":"","content":"They would yet ignore her, and that would mean she doesn't have the desired effect.<br /> <br /> Specially about Elysium, since what usually enforces Elysium is the power of he Keeper, not of the Prince.<br /> <br /> But it could work with some twists. The common Kindred have to think she is powerful to obey, and the Powers that Be must have a reason to let her have her way. As it is described now, she's just a liability, but with some tweaks they can have a better reason to let her be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T04:15:28-07:00","id":621075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/619380-domain-panem-et-circenses?p=620624#post620624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, as things are, they won't. She is a bad compromise, because she hurts even the most basic administrative roles. She is going to upset everyone in the city. This is the single surest way to start a war.<br /> <br /> A character with this kind of behavior needs a safe support to do so, a reason to think she is safe from harm, or to just be spoiled. Because not only he power-players of the city will be upset, the other Kindred will, also. They will want her head. The power-players will see the domain itself falling to pieces as people just ignore or resent her.<br /> <br /> Not to say that this is the behavior of someone who can actually enforce something, and you described a Prince who isn't able to enforce nothing. People would be simply ignoring her, until someone is upset enough to kill her.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the original poster said, that's the point. She is <u>supposed</u> to be eliminated or deposed precisely because it's not going to take the general populace long to figure out that getting on her good side or bad side means nothing. Whether or not she's removed because she alienates enough people to get herself (and possibly her primogen) killed in a coup, or skilled manipulator realizes they can use her to keep the primogen managed and get some competent appointments or changes to the law made, or one or more members of the primogen scale back their feuds (or they eliminate one of their key rivals) in time to keep the city from being grossly mismanaged is more the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:17:30-07:00","id":621285,"title":"","content":"Actually he seems to want this mess to take some time and <u>possibly</u> be intervened by the PCs. He wants a delicate balance in the city, but she offers no balance whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Of course, I can be wrong. In this case, maybe you're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T18:35:36-07:00","id":621776,"title":"","content":"Okay reading these posts I agree she needs some kind of leverage.<br /> <br /> I don't want it to necessarily be physical power. Starting level PCs shouldn't be able to take her in a straight up fight with her normal back up, but any of the Primogen should.<br /> <br /> The fact that if she goes down the Domain goes into all out war will only take her so far, and maybe not as far as I want her to go. She'll likely be deposed in play, but that should be dependant on the actions of the PCs, not on her keeping up her nonsense long enough for the NPCs to get pissed off.<br /> <br /> So here's my question... What other leverage does an incompetent Prince have to keep control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T05:27:22-07:00","id":622072,"title":"","content":"If you want her to be incompetent as Prince, but able to survive the NPCs, so she needs true back-up from the Elders. They need to see her as more than just a little compromise between them, but truly an asset. Of course, that depends on their long term plans.<br /> <br /> Another option is for her to have the back-up of something more powerful than the Elders, but disinterested from their politics. Maybe her sire is a true Methuselah with far reaching power, but little concern for the city itself. She won't intervene in their decisions and fights, but also won't let someone hurt the girl. In that case, she can be just spoiled, and her status as compromise between elders don't need to have a straight correlation with the protection she receives.<br /> <br /> On those cases, the ways for the players to change things is to work on he Elders or the Methuselah, but mostly the Elders. Either upsetting their power balance or just offering a better option will do. Maybe they get rid of her, maybe they just strip her of power and send her to a place better fit for her. The Methuselah should be convinced to take maters on her own hands for her sake or against her, maybe forbidding the Elders from using her, or she can be convinced to remove any protection over the Prince, letting her to be eaten by the wolves.<br /> <br /> You could also play the deception route. This is the <u>perceived</u> state of the city, and most Kindred believe it. But when someone go against her wills, bad things happen, and the Elders do nothing about it. What's going on? She really isn't powerful, but maybe the Elders aren't on the game most people think they are. They can be Dragons doing an experiment on the city about the ability of Kindred to survive, organize and prosper in such conditions. Maybe they decided on a twist for their usual schemes, each one took a couple of pawns to fight for them by proxy and the city is truly a giant living board game for them, so they don't have to risk their necks and can yet take some fun of the process.<br /> <br /> Maybe she isn't so powerful, but she <b>seems</b> to be. She's a less-than-perfect compromise, but with perceived power she can at least keep the city from falling apart. People aren't happy, but they fear her enough to try a coupe. Under the disguise of seemly futility she is truly giving attention to some maters as needed to appease the Elders. And with the entire circus, the vampiric pop of the city is too busy to figure things or organize by themselves. The Elders just have to keep her perceived power. It doesn't solves their enmity, but until they find a way to solve it, she keeps the city running, poorly but without bloodshed. She isn't a happy pawn. She knows she's as good as dead, and the only thing she can do to buy more time is to put a smile on the face and obey.<br /> <br /> Those other scenarios require the players to peel the layers of deceit. Things are still similar to the original idea, but not quite. The distinction is that people thinks it is precisely the original idea, with the add perceived power from her, when she truly has none. At most she have the power to fake real control of the situation.<br /> <br /> For a twist, she can have actual leverage on the Elders. Be it a secret, a weapon or an ally, it isn't something she uses to fool the people, but something she uses to keep an upper hand against her real abusers. She can't use it to full extend, or to actually achieve control of the city, because if she becomes an actual danger she will be targeted for destruction. But once she became the compromise on their petty internal war, she can use it to prevent herself from becoming disposable. The people isn't happy with her rule, but her life actually depends on her being a crappy ruler. She can use said leverage also against the Keepers of Elysium, maybe they're even the Elders or their childes, so she can lift Elysium protection. She's hated by the people, but as long as she plays her cards right, the Elders will protect her. She desperately needs help to actually leave this situation, for even being able to keep it a long time, as soon as she looses leverage against one Elder she will be destroyed.<br /> <br /> With this option you give her one thing to guarantee the Elders protection, and even some measure of power over some other Kindred, but at a cost of being a liability to everyone. The players need to find the leverage and decide what to do with it, from seizing it themselves to destroying it or any other decision. She doesn't need to know the best use for this leverage, she's under so much pressure that she'll just keep running the first plan she could conceive and pray for it to work one more day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T15:02:08-07:00","id":623676,"title":"","content":"After looking through the book, I think there's something you might be rather interested in. One of the Strix in the book, called &quot;Mr. Scratch&quot;(can't remember page number) seems rather perfect for your goals. It possesses the Prince of a Domain, acts in eccentric or depraved ways for its amusement(and to undermine the Kindred's faith in their own social structures) and one of the story seeds listed alongside it involves a incompetent Prince chosen as a compromise becoming possessed and wreaking havoc through messing with those who thought they could control the host before it arrived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T23:37:08-07:00","id":623949,"title":"","content":"Again, the main problem is that <b>FunSize</b> wants the situation to be self-sustained until player intervention. Mr. Scratch creates a situation where resolution is unavoidable. If the players don't act, the circus will eventually come to an end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T08:30:52-07:00","id":624386,"title":"","content":"The PCs -- what are their ties and history in the city? If the covenants or elders are bound to play along to the prince's nonsense, perhaps the coterie isn't for some reason. Perhaps the elders are secretly hoping these neonates will get fed up and act against the Prince. &quot;I could never in a million years advise you to cross the Prince. No, you're not listening. I COULD NEVER in a million years tell you to CROSS THE PRINCE.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you are comfortable with having a powerful threat keeping everyone in line, perhaps the Prince is part of a punishment meted out by said threat because of all the ruckus the elders caused. &quot;You killed my favorite/desecrated my hallowed place/wrecked the ley line/whatever, so you get 99 years of the Lord of Misrule.&quot; There could be a clause where some outsider/vampire embraced during a lunar eclipse/man not of woman born can depose the current Prince, which would make the coterie very valuable. But... they can't be told directly. Or they have to diablerize the Prince. Or the neonates realize that the city will tear itself apart the moment the Prince falls - do they have too much to lose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}